<section class="row justify-content-center"><div class="col-lg-9">
<h1>Acceptable Use Policy</h1><p class="text-muted">Last updated: 21 October 2026</p>
<p>This policy applies to everyone using Choosery/StoreBridge, including sellers, customers, and administrators. The platform may review reports and activity to protect users and maintain a trustworthy marketplace.</p>
<h2 class="h4 mt-4">You must not</h2>
<ul><li>Register with false, misleading, or impersonated identity or contact information, or use another person's phone number or email without authorization.</li><li>Create accounts to evade a suspension, manipulate referrals, spam users, or abuse platform features.</li><li>List illegal, counterfeit, stolen, dangerous, or otherwise prohibited goods, or offer services that violate applicable law.</li><li>Publish deceptive descriptions, fake reviews, fraudulent offers, misleading prices, or false payment confirmations.</li><li>Upload content that infringes intellectual-property, privacy, or other rights, or contains malware or malicious code.</li><li>Attempt unauthorized access, interfere with service availability, scrape or harvest personal information without permission, or bypass security controls.</li><li>Harass, threaten, discriminate against, defraud, or misuse the personal information of another person.</li></ul>
<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Registration and trust signals</h2><p>We may flag repeated registration attempts using an email address or phone number already linked to an account, attempts associated with suspended accounts, or other activity that warrants review. Shared family, business, or organizational contact details can be legitimate; a duplicate signal alone is not proof of abuse and should be assessed in context. We may request clarification or temporarily limit activity while a concern is reviewed.</p>
<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Moderation and enforcement</h2><p>Depending on the circumstances, we may request information, flag or remove listings, limit functionality, suspend or close accounts, preserve relevant audit records, or refer serious concerns to appropriate authorities. We aim to apply measures proportionately and correct mistaken flags when identified. Where appropriate, users may contact support to request a review.</p>
<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Reporting a concern</h2><p>Report suspected abuse, unsafe listings, impersonation, or account compromise through the <a href="/contact.php">Contact page</a>. Include enough detail for us to investigate, but do not send passwords or reset tokens.</p>
<p class="mt-4">This policy may be updated as the platform and applicable law evolve.</p>
